  "final": "I added `GET /api/documents/<id>/download`, and all 9 tests pass, including 4 new ones for this route.\n\n- **Response:** It returns the document content with `Content-Type: application/octet-stream` and `Content-Disposition: attachment`. The filename in that header is sanitized, so a document name can't inject header content. I also set `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`.\n- **Access control:** It looks the document up by the caller's account, using `storage.get_document_for_account`. A document in another account returns 404, the same as a missing one, so callers can't tell which ids exist. Unauthenticated requests get 401 from the existing auth check.\n- **Files:** The handler and route are in `docs_app/routes.py`, the tests are in `docs_app/tests/test_documents.py`, and I added the endpoint to `README.md`.",
